From 330d43642aadfb08a0f8e40a504644f36600aae3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:13:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Strings] Dolby Vision as SDR said where people look
 for it

Every Dolby Vision video can be seen as SDR, one video at a time:
"As SDR (without HDR)" in "Output of this video" of the player
information (O, then OK on that button) or in "Dolby Vision output
(this video)" of the video settings. "Play HDR videos as SDR" leaves
Dolby Vision out on purpose, and a user with a projector without
Dolby Vision (LibreELEC forum, thread 30682, posts 175 and 195) did
not find the choice at all: the help of the settings he read did not
name it.

- The help of "Play HDR videos as SDR" (61111, Estuary 52591), of
  "Show Dolby Vision as HDR10 when the display cannot" (59990, 51697)
  and of "Native Dolby Vision output" (59831, 51771) now say where and
  how.
- The overview of the player information, where a Dolby Vision video
  goes out as HDR10 because of the display or its input (what to do:
  "tv", 52730), adds "As SDR: OK on "Output of this video"".

English first; es_es, es_ar and es_mx translated. No setting moves:
where each one sits is left to the reorganisation of the settings.
